{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Manual AWS Analysis",
  "description": "Triggered when user specifically requests AWS logs analysis or mentions AWS issues",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "onMessage",
    "patterns": ["*analyze aws*", "*aws logs*", "*check aws*", "*aws issue*", "*cloudwatch*", "*lambda error*"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "User requested AWS analysis. Execute comprehensive AWS diagnostics:\n\n1. **Intelligent Log Download**: Run the smart AWS logs script that only downloads problematic logs\n   Command: `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/download-aws-logs.ps1`\n\n2. **Analyze Issues**: Review the downloaded logs and ANALYSIS_SUMMARY.md for:\n   - Error patterns and frequency\n   - Service-specific issues\n   - Performance problems\n   - Configuration issues\n\n3. **Identify Root Causes**: Determine specific problems:\n   - Lambda function errors\n   - API Gateway issues\n   - DynamoDB problems\n   - Authentication failures\n\n4. **Implement Fixes**: Apply necessary solutions:\n   - Code fixes for Lambda functions\n   - Configuration updates\n   - Resource adjustments\n   - Error handling improvements\n\n5. **Auto-Cleanup**: After analysis, clean up logs:\n   Command: `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force temp-logs -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue`\n\n6. **Verify Resolution**: Test fixes and confirm AWS services are working\n\nProvide detailed analysis and implement fixes automatically. No manual review required."
  },
  "workspaceFolderName": "budgetbuddy",
  "shortName": "manual-aws-analysis"
}
